The chosen strategy and rationale are returned to the agent. Final predictions are generated using
combine forecasts(), which produces weighted averages for multi-model ensembles or di-
rect outputs for single-model strategies, and saves Plotly visualizations including historical data,
forecasts, and per-model predictions.
3.1.6 ANOMALY DETECTION.
For anomaly tasks, detect anomalies() applies a 7-method ensemble comprising statistical
(Z-score, Modified Z-score using MAD, rolling statistics), distribution-based (IQR, STL residuals),
and machine learning methods (Isolation Forest, DBSCAN). Majority voting (≥ 3 methods) flags
anomalies, and per-method agreement scores are returned to support transparency.
3.1.7 EXPLAINABILITY TOOLS.
When explanation is requested, the agent invokes tools that compute statistical summaries (recent
trend, 7-day and 1-day averages, comparison to training mean), STL-derived trend and seasonal
strength with residual variance, lag autocorrelations (lags 1, 6, 12, 24), multivariate feature attri-
bution (SHAP values and tree-based feature importance), and Pearson feature correlations with the
target variable. Explanations are synthesized directly from computed numerical outputs, grounding
responses in metrics rather than inferred values.
3.1.8 REPORT GENERATION.
The generate report() tool aggregates all outputs into a structured report containing the data
profile summary, model performance comparison (MAPE, RMSE, MAE per model), ensemble strat-
egy justification, forecast visualizations, and explainability insights when requested